.TH "FLOX\-BUILD\-IMPORT\-NIXPKGS" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-build\-import\-nixpkgs \- Import package definition from nixpkgs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] build import\-nixpkgs
     [\-d=<path>]
     [\-\-force]
     <installable>
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import a package definition from nixpkgs for use in the environment.
This command copies the source code of a package from nixpkgs into the
environment\(cqs \f[CR].flox/pkgs/\f[R] directory, allowing you to
modify and build the package locally.
.PP
The package definition is imported as a Nix expression file at
\f[CR].flox/pkgs/<package>/default.nix\f[R], where \f[CR]<package>\f[R]
is the attribute path of the package (e.g., \f[CR]hello\f[R] for
\f[CR]nixpkgs#hello\f[R]).
.PP
This is useful when you need to:
.IP \(bu 2
Modify a package\(cqs build process
.IP \(bu 2
Apply patches or customizations
.IP \(bu 2
Debug package issues
.IP \(bu 2
Create variants of existing packages
.SS Installable format
The \f[CR]<installable>\f[R] parameter can be specified in one of the
following formats:
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]Attribute path only\f[R]: \f[CR]hello\f[R] (defaults to
\f[CR]nixpkgs#hello\f[R])
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]Flake reference with attribute\f[R]: \f[CR]nixpkgs#hello\f[R]
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]Full flake reference\f[R]: \f[CR]github:nixos/nixpkgs#hello\f[R]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]<installable>\f[R]
The package to import from nixpkgs.
Can be specified as an attribute path (e.g., \f[CR]hello\f[R]) or as a
flake reference with attribute path (e.g., \f[CR]nixpkgs#hello\f[R]).
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-force\f[R]
Overwrite existing package file if it already exists.
Without this flag, the command will fail if the package file already
exists in the environment.
.SS Environment Options
If no environment is specified for an environment command, the
environment in the current directory or the active environment that was
last activated is used.
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Path containing a .flox/ directory.
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Import a simple package
Import the \f[CR]hello\f[R] package from nixpkgs:
.IP
.EX
flox build import\-nixpkgs hello
.EE
.PP
This creates \f[CR].flox/pkgs/hello/default.nix\f[R] with the package
definition.
.SS Import from a specific nixpkgs revision
Import a package from a specific nixpkgs revision:
.IP
.EX
flox build import\-nixpkgs github:nixos/nixpkgs/nixos\-23.11#hello
.EE
.SS Overwrite an existing package
Force import a package, overwriting any existing definition:
.IP
.EX
flox build import\-nixpkgs \-\-force hello
.EE
.SS Import a complex package
Import a package with a nested attribute path:
.IP
.EX
flox build import\-nixpkgs python310Packages.requests
.EE
.PP
This creates
\f[CR].flox/pkgs/python310Packages/requests/default.nix\f[R].
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
This command only works with local environments (not managed or remote
environments)
.IP \(bu 2
The imported package definition is a snapshot of the source code at the
time of import
.IP \(bu 2
You can modify the imported package definition and build it using
\f[CR]flox build\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
The package will be available in the environment\(cqs build context
